[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807101658","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105389#issuecomment-2807101658","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105389","id":2807101658,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nUPja","user":{"login":"jermjar","id":98186820,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdo2RA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98186820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar","html_url":"https://github.com/jermjar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jermjar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T18:23:05Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T18:23:05Z","body":"After studying some of the behind the scenes code and looking at the Remote Scene, I was able to find a workaround to this.\n\nWhen looking in the Remote Scene, I discovered that there is an extra TabBar being created that is named `@TabBar@2`.  This is what needs focus in order to navigate the tabs.  There are a few steps that need to be taken for this workaround:\n- Set the `focus_mode` of each custom tab to `None` (in the reproduction project, this would be the `Options` and `Inputs` tabs)\n- Set the button(s) that want to navigate to the tabs to have no neighbor in the direction they need to go (in the reproduction project, you would set `VolumeHSlider` to have no `focus_neighbor_top` in the `Options` tab)\n\nThis workaround ensures that the only Control node available to grab focus of is the extra TabBar being created\n\nAlthough this fix makes sense when looking into it, I still think this deserves attention, as it isn't intuitive.  Focus and functionality should be on the things the user is creating (in this case, the `Options` and `Inputs` Panel tabs that I created), and not a magical one behind the scenes that needs focus.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807101658/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807836477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105389#issuecomment-2807836477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105389","id":2807836477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nXC89","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T00:19:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T00:25:20Z","body":"The main reason is that you assigned the control **itself** as the focus neighbor. Also note that hidden controls do not grab focus. That is, it must be visible before it **can** grab focus.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807836477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]